  "comments": "<p>A few different dies are known. There are many differences between dies, here marked those, which are enough for attribution.<br><br><i>Obverse</i><br>Die <strong>1</strong> - small embossed and spaced grains, at the bottom stalks snuggle to short ribbon.<br>Die <strong>2</strong> - large flat grains, at the bottom stalks protrude from long ribbon.<br><br><i>Reverse</i><br>Die 1956 - embossed font, small serifs at the right top of K to MARK.<br>Die 1962 - flat font, small serifs at the right top of K to MARK.<br>Die 1963 - flat font, very long serif at the right top of K to MARK.<br>Picture: © Images courtesy of Alexandr Prokofyev.<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/621ea3efaef3e.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/621ea3efaef3e.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br><i>Combinations</i><br>Obverse Die <strong>1</strong> + Reverse 1956.<br>Obverse Die <strong>1</strong> + Reverse 1962.<br>Obverse Die <strong>2</strong> + Reverse 1963.</p>",
